 "$comment": "The system key registry: one entry per hestia.conf key, class and default. Read at runtime from the tree (deliberately, see STRUCTURE.md); never copied to the box. betreiber = a human sets it, the repair fills an absent or empty key with the default, an update never touches it. system = the consequence of an action, written by commands; the repair never fills it (a verification in the smoke says whether it agrees with the box), an update may set it by manifest entry. tokens = a comma-separated token set; token_fn names the function that adds or removes one token (Phase 2 calls it, 1a only checks it exists). Guarded by sysreg_check (include/sysreg.sh), run by the smoke and by CI.",
